-- §9 forbids trailing whitespace: a comment that pushes a lambda's `->` onto
-- its own line must not leave the space that was going to separate it at the
-- end of the line above. (A binding's `=` or `<-` cannot be pushed so: in a
-- block its head is on one line, language.md §12.2.)
f r =
    render r
        (λz
        -- why the lambda
        -> z
        )
